1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,778
107 trillion won in three months.

2
00:00:01,778 --> 00:00:03,815
That's Samsung Electronics' operating profit

3
00:00:03,815 --> 00:00:04,880
from July to September.

4
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:08,180
That's more than a trillion won a day.

5
00:00:08,370 --> 00:00:09,980
Weekends and holidays included.

6
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:16,680
Yet the stock is down 42% from its high of 37만 4천 원 in 2026년 6월.

7
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:17,662
Record profits,

8
00:00:17,662 --> 00:00:19,850
and the share price heading the other way.

9
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:23,036
Ever tried buying a computer this year and been

10
00:00:23,036 --> 00:00:24,310
shocked by memory prices?

11
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:28,115
That memory is why Samsung is making so much money,

12
00:00:28,115 --> 00:00:30,000
and also why its stock is shaky.

13
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:34,013
So today, a short class on memory chips.

14
00:00:34,013 --> 00:00:35,860
No exam, so just relax.

15
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:38,009
Why AI is hoovering up memory,

16
00:00:38,009 --> 00:00:40,477
how Samsung fell behind and caught up,

17
00:00:40,477 --> 00:00:43,270
and why the stock falls while profits peak.

18
00:00:43,470 --> 00:00:47,680
Plus three numbers to watch at the October 29 earnings.

19
00:00:48,490 --> 00:00:50,180
First, what memory actually is.

20
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:53,569
Think of a computer as a study room.

21
00:00:53,569 --> 00:00:55,510
The processor is the brain.

22
00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:58,529
DRAM is the desk where you spread out what you're working on,

23
00:00:58,529 --> 00:01:00,840
and NAND is the bookshelf where things are stored.

24
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:05,100
Phones, laptops and servers all need this desk.

25
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:09,260
And Samsung sells more of it than anyone in the world.

26
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:13,053
Even a genius wastes time swapping books in and

27
00:01:13,053 --> 00:01:14,900
out if the desk is too small.

28
00:01:15,090 --> 00:01:16,482
So the faster the brain gets,

29
00:01:16,482 --> 00:01:18,450
the bigger and faster the desk has to be.

30
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:22,490
So how much desk does a student called AI need?

31
00:01:23,290 --> 00:01:25,900
A very wide, very fast desk.

32
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:30,352
AI is a student with thousands of books open at once.

33
00:01:30,352 --> 00:01:34,830
Every line it writes pulls a huge amount of numbers off the desk.

34
00:01:35,030 --> 00:01:39,153
So Nvidia attached a special desk right next to its AI chip.

35
00:01:39,153 --> 00:01:41,490
That's HBM, high bandwidth memory.

36
00:01:42,290 --> 00:01:44,439
HBM stacks DRAM chips twelve floors high,

37
00:01:44,439 --> 00:01:45,382
like an apartment,

38
00:01:45,382 --> 00:01:48,160
with holes drilled through each floor like elevators.

39
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:52,257
The latest HBM4 has 2,048 data lanes.

40
00:01:52,257 --> 00:01:54,890
A PC memory stick has 64.

41
00:01:55,690 --> 00:01:58,888
The buyers are Big Tech. Amazon, Alphabet,

42
00:01:58,888 --> 00:02:02,011
Microsoft and Meta plan about 735 billion

43
00:02:02,011 --> 00:02:04,905
dollars of capital spending this year.

44
00:02:04,905 --> 00:02:06,580
Over 970 trillion won.

45
00:02:07,380 --> 00:02:10,382
Each new AI chip came with a bigger desk.

46
00:02:10,382 --> 00:02:12,579
Nvidia's Rubin, out this year,

47
00:02:12,579 --> 00:02:13,970
uses next-gen HBM4.

48
00:02:14,170 --> 00:02:15,427
Memory prices jumped.

49
00:02:15,427 --> 00:02:17,880
TrendForce expected general DRAM contract

50
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:20,693
prices to rise 90 to 95 percent in Q1 2026 from

51
00:02:20,693 --> 00:02:21,950
the previous quarter.

52
00:02:22,750 --> 00:02:24,989
But wait. AI buys HBM,

53
00:02:24,989 --> 00:02:29,570
so why did PC and phone DRAM get pricier too?

54
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:33,808
Making the same amount of HBM takes about three

55
00:02:33,808 --> 00:02:36,807
times the silicon wafers of regular DRAM,

56
00:02:36,807 --> 00:02:38,270
according to Micron.

57
00:02:38,470 --> 00:02:40,061
The more HBM a fab makes,

58
00:02:40,061 --> 00:02:42,860
the fewer wafers are left for ordinary DRAM.

59
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:47,419
It's like a bakery using triple the flour for fancy cakes,

60
00:02:47,419 --> 00:02:50,400
so bread runs short and bread prices rise too.

61
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:51,320
In September,

62
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:53,978
the PC DRAM fixed contract price hit 26 dollars,

63
00:02:53,978 --> 00:02:55,750
up another 4 percent in a month.

64
00:02:56,550 --> 00:03:00,410
But Samsung wasn't the first to ace the HBM test.

65
00:03:01,210 --> 00:03:04,067
Samsung failed to pass Nvidia's HBM quality

66
00:03:04,067 --> 00:03:07,390
tests on time and fell behind SK hynix and Micron.

67
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:09,114
On October 8, 2024,

68
00:03:09,114 --> 00:03:13,100
Samsung's chip chief issued a rare public apology.

69
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:20,070
The stock fell to 49,900 won on November 14 that year.

70
00:03:20,270 --> 00:03:24,296
Then in Q4 2025 it passed Nvidia's 12-high HBM3E test,

71
00:03:24,296 --> 00:03:28,770
and in February 2026 began shipping next-gen HBM4 to Nvidia.

72
00:03:29,570 --> 00:03:33,253
Had you bought 100 million won at that low,

73
00:03:33,253 --> 00:03:36,080
it would be worth 4억 3천만 원 today.

74
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:39,011
The report card changed too.

75
00:03:39,011 --> 00:03:43,120
Operating profit was 6.6 trillion won for all of 2023.

76
00:03:43,310 --> 00:03:46,412
This year, 107.4 trillion in Q3 alone.

77
00:03:46,412 --> 00:03:50,330
Sixteen times 2023's full year, in three months.

78
00:03:51,130 --> 00:03:54,220
SK hynix is still top of the HBM class,

79
00:03:54,220 --> 00:03:56,360
with 50 percent in Q2 2026,

80
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:58,420
per Counterpoint Research.

81
00:03:58,630 --> 00:04:02,558
Samsung jumped from 21 to 33 percent,

82
00:04:02,558 --> 00:04:08,610
cutting the gap from 37 points to 17 in a single quarter.

83
00:04:09,410 --> 00:04:12,150
But there are more students in the memory class.

84
00:04:12,950 --> 00:04:17,712
In overall DRAM, Samsung leads with 38 percent,

85
00:04:17,712 --> 00:04:21,460
then SK hynix at 25 and Micron at 24.

86
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:23,778
Watch the fourth line.

87
00:04:23,778 --> 00:04:27,050
China's CXMT now holds 10 percent.

88
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:30,762
Under 1 percent three years ago,

89
00:04:30,762 --> 00:04:34,130
4 percent a year ago, 10 percent now.

90
00:04:34,330 --> 00:04:37,540
It reported about 53 trillion won in revenue

91
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:39,364
for January to September.

92
00:04:39,364 --> 00:04:42,210
The new kid is already fourth in class.

93
00:04:43,010 --> 00:04:45,533
Micron is also lifting HBM wafer output from 40

94
00:04:45,533 --> 00:04:48,003
to 50 thousand a month last year to around 100

95
00:04:48,003 --> 00:04:49,130
thousand by year-end.

96
00:04:49,930 --> 00:04:51,402
Everyone is building.

97
00:04:51,402 --> 00:04:55,537
SK hynix opens its first Yongin cleanroom in February 2027,

98
00:04:55,537 --> 00:04:58,550
and Samsung targets 2028 for Pyeongtaek P5.

99
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:01,922
CXMT is forecast to grow from 350 thousand

100
00:05:01,922 --> 00:05:05,160
wafers a month to 500 thousand by end-2028.

101
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:10,026
Memory has always sung the same song. Shortage,

102
00:05:10,026 --> 00:05:11,842
everyone builds fabs,

103
00:05:11,842 --> 00:05:14,870
then oversupply and falling prices.

104
00:05:15,070 --> 00:05:18,840
Gartner expects DRAM prices to fall from late 2027.

105
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:23,350
Micron says the 2028 shortage will be worse than this year's.

106
00:05:24,140 --> 00:05:27,640
So why is the stock down 42% at record profits?

107
00:05:28,450 --> 00:05:31,798
Memory fabs cost about the same even when prices drop.

108
00:05:31,798 --> 00:05:34,340
Say a chip sold for 100 now sells for 90.

109
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:36,181
With costs fixed at 50,

110
00:05:36,181 --> 00:05:39,321
profit falls from 50 to 40, down 20 percent.

111
00:05:39,321 --> 00:05:42,390
Prices fall 10, profits fall twice as much.

112
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:46,246
So markets watch the speed of price gains.

113
00:05:46,246 --> 00:05:49,313
From a forecast 90-plus percent in Q1 to 4

114
00:05:49,313 --> 00:05:51,430
percent in September's month.

115
00:05:51,630 --> 00:05:53,507
Still rising, but slower.

116
00:05:53,507 --> 00:05:56,810
Stocks price that in before profits show it.

117
00:05:57,610 --> 00:05:59,516
The last cycle went the same way.

118
00:05:59,516 --> 00:06:02,173
The stock fell from 96,800 won in January 2021

119
00:06:02,173 --> 00:06:04,367
to the 52 thousands by September 2022,

120
00:06:04,367 --> 00:06:06,100
while profits were still high.

121
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:09,431
Then in 2023, when profit fell 85 percent,

122
00:06:09,431 --> 00:06:11,220
the stock actually rose.

123
00:06:12,020 --> 00:06:12,751
Last week,

124
00:06:12,751 --> 00:06:15,677
when Meta fell 7 percent after earnings,

125
00:06:15,677 --> 00:06:18,530
Samsung dropped 4 percent the same day.

126
00:06:18,730 --> 00:06:21,097
Meta spent 2.1 billion dollars more on

127
00:06:21,097 --> 00:06:24,087
investment than it made in operating cash in Q3.

128
00:06:24,087 --> 00:06:26,080
The card bill beat the paycheck.

129
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:29,580
So how should you value a company like this?

130
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:33,161
Warren Buffett's teacher Benjamin Graham warned

131
00:06:33,161 --> 00:06:36,120
against valuing cyclical firms on their best year.

132
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:39,009
Use average earnings across good and bad years,

133
00:06:39,009 --> 00:06:41,470
leave growth out, and value conservatively.

134
00:06:42,270 --> 00:06:46,920
Samsung earned about 2만 2,700원 per share over the past year.

135
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:50,090
Averaged over good and bad years,

136
00:06:50,090 --> 00:06:52,250
it's about about 6,900원.

137
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:57,329
Ten times that average gives 6만 9천 원 a share.

138
00:06:57,329 --> 00:07:00,650
The price of 21만 5천 원 is 3.1x that.

139
00:07:00,850 --> 00:07:02,722
Not a buy or sell call.

140
00:07:02,722 --> 00:07:06,140
It means the price assumes the boom lasts.

141
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:09,260
So the ValueNote score is 41.

142
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:12,435
Financial strength scores 71,

143
00:07:12,435 --> 00:07:15,000
but price scores only 23.

144
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:17,570
Recalculated the same way,

145
00:07:17,570 --> 00:07:20,075
the score on October 20, 2022 was 49.

146
00:07:20,075 --> 00:07:23,730
100 million won then is about 4억 원 now with dividends.

147
00:07:23,930 --> 00:07:27,317
But back then the stock had already nearly halved.

148
00:07:27,317 --> 00:07:29,350
Now profits are at their peak.

149
00:07:30,150 --> 00:07:32,382
Of course, this could be wrong.

150
00:07:32,382 --> 00:07:36,414
As more memory is sold on multi-year contracts like HBM,

151
00:07:36,414 --> 00:07:38,070
profits may swing less.

152
00:07:38,270 --> 00:07:40,691
Then the historical average is too low,

153
00:07:40,691 --> 00:07:43,050
and the stock could actually be cheap.

154
00:07:43,860 --> 00:07:48,310
ValueNote runs this same calculation daily for 600-plus companies.

155
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:52,390
Finally, three numbers for this week's earnings.

156
00:07:53,190 --> 00:07:55,324
SK hynix reports on the 28th,

157
00:07:55,324 --> 00:07:58,340
Alphabet and Microsoft early on the 29th.

158
00:07:58,540 --> 00:08:03,320
Samsung holds its Q3 earnings call on the morning of the 29th.

159
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:04,484
First,

160
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:07,884
how much Big Tech will raise capital spending next year.

161
00:08:07,884 --> 00:08:10,070
That's the AI student's desk budget.

162
00:08:10,270 --> 00:08:13,083
Second, how much HBM4 Samsung sold.

163
00:08:13,083 --> 00:08:16,780
Are the grades still rising after the apology?

164
00:08:16,990 --> 00:08:19,399
Third, the speed of DRAM price gains.

165
00:08:19,399 --> 00:08:20,701
If it keeps slowing,

166
00:08:20,701 --> 00:08:23,110
the stock may move before profits do.

167
00:08:23,910 --> 00:08:27,671
To sum up: AI needs a wide, fast desk,

168
00:08:27,671 --> 00:08:29,750
and that desk is HBM.

169
00:08:29,950 --> 00:08:34,560
Samsung climbed back to 33 percent of HBM after its apology.

170
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:38,171
But memory stocks watch the speed of price gains before profits.

171
00:08:38,171 --> 00:08:40,410
That's why the stock fell at peak profits.

172
00:08:41,210 --> 00:08:44,830
If this class helped, please subscribe and like.

173
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:49,040
Turn on notifications to get our post-earnings analysis first.

174
00:08:49,250 --> 00:08:52,747
Watch our SK hynix episode too,

175
00:08:52,747 --> 00:08:58,050
the top student in memory. Thanks for watching.
